<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand I of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1793">1793</a>–<a href="/years/1875">1875</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-habsburg-lorraine">House of Habsburg-Lorraine</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> was emperor from 1835 to 1848, also king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyria">Illyria</a>. Suffering from epilepsy, he left government to a regency council dominated by Metternich. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolutions-of-1848">revolutions of 1848</a> he was persuaded to abdicate in favour of his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-i">Franz Joseph I</a>, and he lived quietly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-austria.jpg" alt="Ferdinand I of Austria" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eduard Edlinger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaiser_Ferdinand_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Ferdinand was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Francis II, Holy Roman Emperor</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. His parents were double first cousins, sharing all four grandparents, so that he descended twice from each of his four great-grandparents. Possibly as a result of this closeness, he had hydrocephalus, neurological problems including epilepsy, and a speech impediment. He was educated by Baron Josef Kalasanz von Erberg and his wife, Countess Josephine von Attems. He married Maria Anna of Savoy, the sixth child of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-i-of-sardinia">Victor Emmanuel I of Sardinia</a>, and the couple had no children.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>Ferdinand succeeded his father Francis I on 2 March 1835 as Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, where he was Ferdinand V, and ruler of the other lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy. He was also president of the German Confederation until 12 July 1848. Because of severe epilepsy he was thought unable to rule, and his father's will told him to consult his uncle Archduke Louis on internal policy and urged him to be guided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klemens-von-metternich">Prince Metternich</a>, the foreign minister. Although he was never declared incapacitated, a Regent's Council of Archduke Louis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-anton-von-kolowrat-liebsteinsky">Count Kolowrat</a> and Metternich steered the government.</p><p>Later accounts have depicted him as feeble-minded, yet he kept a coherent and legible diary and is said to have had a sharp wit. He suffered as many as twenty seizures a day, which severely limited his ability to govern. His good nature earned him the nickname The Benign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, the Czech form Ferdinand Dobrotivý. He was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a> to be crowned as such and the last ruler crowned with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-crown-of-lombardy">Iron Crown of Lombardy</a> as King of Lombardy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a>.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>When the revolutionaries of 1848 marched on the palace, Ferdinand is supposed to have asked Metternich what was happening and, on hearing that a revolution had begun, to have replied, &quot;But are they allowed to do that?&quot; Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-zu-schwarzenberg">Felix of Schwarzenberg</a> persuaded him to abdicate in favour of his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-i">Franz Joseph</a>. The next in line, his brother Franz Karl, renounced his rights in favour of his son at his wife Sophie's urging. Ferdinand abdicated on 2 December 1848, and Franz Joseph reigned for the next 68 years. In his diary he described the new emperor kneeling for his blessing. He lived in Hradčany Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> until his death on 29 June 1875, and is buried in the Imperial Crypt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Ferdinand I of Austria” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/czech-republic">the Czech Republic</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1846" aria-label="Vienna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4931 477 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ferdinand I of Austria"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5381 747h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1846">What was here in 1846? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
